<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Kazakh 12-mth T-bill av yield falls to 15.74 pct.</title>
<headline>Kazakh 12-mth T-bill av yield falls to 15.74 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on an issue of twelve-month MKM discount Treasury bills fell to 15.74 percent at auction on June 2 from 22.59 percent at the last auction on May 5, the National Bank said.</p>
<p>Details of the auction:</p>
<p>					   June 2	     May 5</p>
<p> Series number			 KZ4CK0406983     KZ4CK0705988</p>
<p> Issue volume (million tenge)	  450		  400</p>
<p> Bids (nominal, bln tenge)	 2.53		 2.03</p>
<p> Sold (nominal, million tenge)	 460		  500</p>
<p> Average price			 86.40 pct	  81.57</p>
<p> Average yield			 15.74		22.59</p>
<p> Tenor				   364 days	   364 days</p>
<p> Maturity				June 4, 1998     May 7, 1998</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom, +7 3272 509410</p>
</text>
